NOT RUN (the person who wrote the sheet)
  - THE STOP is bar 1's far extreme (an up gap's bar-1 low, a down gap's bar-1 high), exactly on it with no extra tick; the video does not say how far beyond it. Floored at 0.25 x ATR(14) of the 5-minute bars and two ticks.
  - THE ORDER rests at the gap's near edge until it fills, a bar closes beyond the gap's far edge, or the pass's last 5 minutes (10:55, 13:25, 15:53); the video does not say how long it waits.
  - 'A gap forms through the candle': the engine counts the gap when its middle bar trades at the candle's level and closes beyond it; the gap's own zone may lie above, around or below the level.
  - THE CAP: one SIGNAL per session pass (the first gap that counts, either side, whether or not it fills); three passes (09:30-11:00, 11:00-13:30, 13:30-15:58), so a day can hold up to 3 trades, and a midday or afternoon trade may start while an earlier pass's trade is still open.
  - MIDDAY AND AFTERNOON: the video teaches the morning only; in those passes the gap's three bars must all lie inside that pass, and the levels are the morning candle's.
  - The 1-minute SCALP of the same video is NOT this sheet.
  - FULLY BLIND: no open_fvg sheet or card has ever been run, so no month of this family was read.
  - COSTS AND FILLS: the engine's own (1 tick of slippage, $4 a round turn, tick replay, strict limit fills).
  - THE TEST DAYS (2025-07-01 on) ARE NOT READ by this sheet: build days only.
  - FLAT: every trade is flat by 15:58 ET (13:13 on half days).

ALSO TRUE OF THE RUN (the lane)
  - CAPPED PER SESSION PASS, NOT PER DAY: max_trades 1 counts inside each pass (3 passes: nyam, mid, pm), so a day can hold up to 3 trades; a family's own loss or trade count (none) counts inside one pass too.
  - The passes are independent: a trade of one pass may still be open when another pass enters (one position at a time holds inside a pass only).
  - Every trade is flat by 15:58 ET (13:13 on an equity half day); no entry in the last 5 minutes of a pass.
  - Costs: $4.00 a round turn and 1 tick of slippage on market and stop fills, 1 contract (the engine's own).
  - The stop is the family's structure level of each entry (its size differs from trade to trade; the engine never puts it closer than two ticks or 0.25 ATR); `stop_val` is not used.

HONEST LIMITS
  - One video's rule, read on the build days (2021-09-22 .. 2025-06-30): in-sample.
  - The family's settings and the exits are the video's own: nothing was tuned, searched or picked.
  - The neighbours are shown to see how fragile the rule is; they are not alternatives to choose from.
  - The unseen days (2025-07-01 on) were not read: a person has to ask for that, and it is read once.
  - The random entries are the pipeline's own (any bar of the session pass, matched by day and pass): they do not wait for the family's entry window.
